### 2. Optimized Service Implementation

**File:** `com.tcs.fincore.CommonMasterService.service.CommonMasterServiceImpl.java`

Instead of manually using `objectMapper.writeValueAsString`, we let Spring handle the conversion. This is cleaner and more performant as it avoids redundant string allocations.

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public Map<Long, Double> getOrGenerateLhoSummary(Long id) {
    log.info("Processing LHO Summary request for ID: {}", id);

    // 1. Check Cache
    Optional<LhoTransferSummary> cached = lhoSummaryRepository.findById(id);
    if (cached.isPresent()) {
        try {
            // Convert the stored CLOB String back into a Map for the response
            return objectMapper.readValue(cached.get().getPayload(), new TypeReference<Map<Long, Double>>() {});
        } catch (Exception e) {
            log.error("Error parsing cached summary for ID: {}", id);
        }
    }

    // 2. Cache Miss: Database Aggregation
    log.info("Generating new aggregation for ID: {}", id);
    List<Object[]> aggregatedData = plTransferRepository.getAggregatedSummary();

    if (aggregatedData.isEmpty()) {
        return Collections.emptyMap(); // Return {} instead of throwing error if preferred
    }

    // 3. Map result
    Map<Long, Double> summaryMap = aggregatedData.stream()
            .collect(Collectors.toMap(
                    row -> ((Number) row[0]).longValue(),
                    row -> ((Number) row[1]).doubleValue()
            ));

    // 4. Async/Background Save (Optional Optimization)
    // We save the JSON string to the DB CLOB for next time
    try {
        String jsonPayload = objectMapper.writeValueAsString(summaryMap);
        lhoSummaryRepository.save(new LhoTransferSummary(id, jsonPayload));
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.warn("Failed to cache summary, but returning data anyway.");
    }

    return summaryMap;
}

```

